<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CABINET SPOKESMAN LEAVES TO JOIN CHEMAPOL, SUCCESSOR NAMED.</title>
<headline>CABINET SPOKESMAN LEAVES TO JOIN CHEMAPOL, SUCCESSOR NAMED.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech government spokesman Vadim Petrov said on Wednesday he would resign his post at the end of this week to join industrial conglomerate Chemapol Group a.s. as director of communications and organisational management.</p>
<p>Petrov said he will be replaced by 34-year-old Ivo Strejcek, an English and Czech language teacher at a secondary school in the southeastern town of Zdar Nad Sazavou.</p>
<p>Strejcek is a member of the centre-right senior coalition Civic Democratic Party (ODS) led by Prime minister Vaclav Klaus.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
